-- title:
--   Γ₀(3) is generated by T, U and -1
-- statement:
--   Let $U$ be an element of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ whose underlying integer $2\times 2$ matrix is $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ -3 & 1\end{pmatrix}$. The assertion is an equality of subgroups of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$: the subgroup generated by the three-element set consisting of `ModularGroup.T`, that is the translation matrix $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ 0 & 1\end{pmatrix}$, of $U$, and of the central element $-1$, coincides with the congruence subgroup `CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 3`, namely the subgroup of those elements of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ whose lower-left entry is congruent to $0$ modulo $3$. Since the equality is of subgroups, both inclusions are contained in it: each of $T$, $U$ and $-1$ has lower-left entry divisible by $3$, and conversely every matrix in $\Gamma_0(3)$ is a word in these three elements and their inverses.
--
--   This is the classical determination, going back to Rademacher, of generators for $\Gamma_0(3)$: the stabiliser $T$ of the cusp $\infty$, the stabiliser $U$ of the cusp $0$ (a conjugate of $T^{-1}$ by the Fricke involution $W_3 = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -1 \\ 3 & 0\end{pmatrix}$), together with the centre. It is used in [`ModularForm.exists_weight_one_gamma1_three_slash_fricke_eq_smul`](thm.html#ModularForm.exists_weight_one_gamma1_three_slash_fricke_eq_smul), where the behaviour of a weight one form of level $3$ under the Fricke involution is pinned down by checking finitely many generators.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CongruenceSubgroup_closure_T_U_neg_one_eq_Gamma0_three.lean

